A||||8||WampusCat||GM SYNCHROMESH OIL||||1||
Z||000000||WampusCat||12-15-2000||07:12 PM||||My local Pontiac dealer wants $9.20 for a quart of this stuff. It's what my Hayes(sp?)manual calls for for the 88 5spd GT.  Are people using cheaper alternatives?  I know it's only 2 qts and you don't have to change it often but $9.20?!?!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-15-2000||07:18 PM||||I used to use Mobil-1 5w30 in my Fieros but switch last year to Syncromesh.  The transmissions in both cars I switched to Syncromesh shift smoother and seem quieter since I changed over.  It is expensive, but it really seems to make a difference in my cars.  <P>I recommend the GM fluid highly.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||12-15-2000||09:25 PM||||I did mine with the Syncromesh GM fluid and I only needed one quart. $10 is not really that expensive when you consider you only need one quart. An oil change cost more than that. <P>I would never deviate from the manufacturers recommendations because there is allot of engineering that goes into those recommendations and why would you want to take a risk with your rare 5-speed just to save a coupe of bucks. Just do it!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||12-15-2000||10:26 PM||||i asked about this a few weeks back. it looks like auto tranny fluid in mine. is this syncromesh stuff red?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||12-16-2000||12:36 AM||||There are some very nice tranny fluid product out there, and they make a noticable difference in the shift feel. Most of them have good replutations, but there are a few strange stories about metallurgical incompatibilty. Just make sure that the spec for the oil you use comply with or exceeds what is stated in the owners manual. Redline MTL, BG Syncromesh and Amsoil Series 2000 are popular.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WampusCat||12-16-2000||08:46 AM||||OK I bought some of the Synchromesh and I'll see how it works although it shifts fine now.  Trouble is, I don't know what's in there now.  I just bought the car and the prev. owner hadn't changed it in the two years he owned the car.  The synchro is a golden-brown color.  I suspect a red fluid would be dextron.<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>i asked about this a few weeks back. it looks like auto tranny fluid in mine. is this syncromesh stuff red?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||12-16-2000||10:16 AM||||From what I heard, the synchromesh is GM's synthtic lube, and really good stuff.  This is the only stuff that is recommended in my Tremec TKO that I'm running in the 5.0, and haven't had a problem yet.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||WampusCat||12-16-2000||01:24 PM||||A friend steered me to the Penzoil website <A HREF="http://www.pennzoil.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pennzoil.com/</A>  and they have a product called "Penzoil Synchromesh Fluid."  According to their site, it meets GM standards and is suitable for transaxles and transmissions requiring GM part #12345349.  He said it's about $4.00 but my local parts store didn't have any.  Oh well, something to look for next time.<P>Steve||||reg||1
Z||000008||Nashco||12-16-2000||10:42 PM||||My dad has worked at several GM dealerships, including a Pontiac dealership.  He worked on a TON of Fieros during 89-90 doing mostly recalls.  I asked him what he thought about this, because I'm going to replace the fluid in my Getrag soon(I just bought it).  He said to use GM Syncromesh, no matter the cost.  He said it is by far the best stuff for these trannies, and will usually help shifting if your synchros are getting worn out too.<P>Anyway, is 10 bucks difference really that big of a deal guys?  Think how much your tranny costs to rebuild, how many miles you want to get out of it, and how often you change the fluid.  Now, does 10 bucks seem like such a big deal?<P>This is right along the lines of, "Is it ok for me to use the 69 cent oil instead of the $1.89 oil?"<P>Please, respect your Fiero, change the fluids properly(mileage and replacement fluids).<P>Thanks<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 12-16-2000).]||||reg||1
